Grandma’s Story: The Two Seeds (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100153

Grandma adjusted her glasses and said, “Here’s another story for you.”

“Once, there were two seeds lying in the same soil.

The first seed said, ‘I want to grow! I want to see the sun, feel the breeze, and become a big plant.’

So it pushed itself up through the soil and began to grow.

The second seed was afraid.

It said, ‘What if I get hurt? What if something eats me? I will stay safe here.’

Days passed.

The first seed grew into a strong plant with green leaves.

The second seed stayed under the soil, doing nothing.

One day, a bird came and ate the second seed.

Grandma looked at the children and said softly, ‘Those who are afraid to try often miss their chance.’”

💖 Moral:

Be brave and take chances to grow.
